   "source": [
    "# Spatial Void Feature Extraction — X-ray Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "Extracts location-aware void features from the hellastudy X-ray images for the ChipVoid-Thermal classification project.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pipeline (follows Part I of the hellastudy, §IV.A, Fig. 5 — \"average image subtracted from the DUT, then thresholding\"):**\n",
    "1. Group X-ray images by LED type.\n",
    "2. Per LED type → **register** all images (shift, rotation, scale) and build a void-less *reference image* (median of the registered images).\n",
    "3. Auto-detect pad regions from the reference (pads are the darkest connected components). The largest-area component is the thermal pad for 3-pad LEDs; 2-pad LEDs have no thermal pad.\n",
    "4. For each DUT, fit the reference to the DUT **locally** (brightness, contrast, sub-pixel shift, blur) and subtract → residual where voids are highlighted and internal structure is suppressed. Hysteresis threshold → binary void mask.\n",
    "5. Validate the void ratio of every LED against the paper's own result, `data/raw/CrackVoid Ratios/Xray Void Ratio.csv`.\n",
    "6. Compute spatial features per pad, in pad-normalized coordinates. Aggregate by pad role (thermal vs. electrical).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data:** `../data/raw/XRay/XRay/<LED_TYPE>/XRay_<LED_TYPE>_<PASTE>_Panel<N>_LED<NN>_<TSC>TSC.jpg`. 200 images per LED type × 9 types = 1,800 total, all at 0 TSC (initial inspection). Six of them are placeholder pictures that only say \"Missing\".\n",
    "\n",
    "**Modality:** X-ray only. SAM is not required for initial void characterization (Part I: *\"SAM is less sensitive for initial void detection than X-ray\"*)."
   ]
  },
