   "source": [
    "_FNAME_RE = re.compile(\n",
    "    r\"XRay_(?P<led_type>[^_]+)_(?P<paste>[^_]+)_Panel(?P<panel>\\d+)_LED(?P<led_num>\\d+)_(?P<tsc>\\d+)TSC\\.jpg\",\n",
    "    re.IGNORECASE,\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def parse_filename(fname):\n",
    "    m = _FNAME_RE.match(fname)\n",
    "    if not m:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    d = m.groupdict()\n",
    "    d[\"panel\"]    = int(d[\"panel\"])\n",
    "    d[\"led_num\"]  = int(d[\"led_num\"])\n",
    "    d[\"tsc\"]      = int(d[\"tsc\"])\n",
    "    d[\"unit_id\"]  = f\"{d['led_type']}_{d['paste']}_P{d['panel']}_L{d['led_num']:02d}\"\n",
    "    return d\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_led_type(led_type, tsc=0):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Load all images for one LED type at a given TSC. Returns (images, metadata_rows).\"\"\"\n",
    "    folder = DATA_DIR / led_type\n",
    "    images, meta = [], []\n",
    "    for f in sorted(folder.iterdir()):\n",
    "        info = parse_filename(f.name)\n",
    "        if info is None or info[\"tsc\"] != tsc:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        im = cv2.imread(str(f), cv2.IMREAD_GRAYSCALE)\n",
    "        if im is None:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        images.append(im)\n",
    "        info[\"file\"] = f.name\n",
    "        meta.append(info)\n",
    "    return images, meta\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Smoke test on one LED type\n",
    "images, meta = load_led_type(\"FC-SP3\")\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(images)} FC-SP3 images at TSC=0, example dims={images[0].shape}\")\n",
    "pd.DataFrame(meta).head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "095c2371",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Per-LED-type reference image (Part I method)\n",
    "\n",
    "Each LED type gets its **own** reference image, computed from only that type's 200 units:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Skip placeholder pictures (\"Missing\").\n",
    "2. Register every image to a template: full-range template search (some LEDs sit tens of pixels off-centre) → ECC refinement for shift + rotation → ECC affine for scale (magnification differs by about ±1.5 % between shots).\n",
    "3. Reference = per-pixel **median** of the registered images; repeat the registration against that median.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why this matters:** a translation-only alignment that gives up beyond 8 px leaves pad edges and internal structures misaligned by a few pixels. After subtraction those edges are brighter than the reference and get counted as voids.\n",
    "\n",
    "**What the reference should look like:** pads, bumps and wire bonds sharp; voids gone (they are at random places, so the median removes them)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 131,
   "id": "7a70167f",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-11-15T15:40:08.273265Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2026-11-15T15:40:08.273002Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2026-11-15T15:40:16.161864Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2026-11-15T15:40:16.160566Z"
    }
   },
   "outputs": [
