   "source": [
    "def calibrate_threshold(ctx, Ts=range(6, 21)):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Sweep the threshold T for one LED type and compare the per-LED void ratio with the CSV.\n",
    "    Returns a table (T, mean absolute error in %-points, Pearson r, mean ratio ours / CSV).\"\"\"\n",
    "    csv = pd.DataFrame(ctx[\"meta\"]).merge(gt_df, on=_KEY, how=\"left\")[\"csv_void_ratio\"].values\n",
    "    use = ctx[\"ok\"] & ~np.isnan(csv)\n",
    "    resid = {i: void_residual(ctx, i) for i in np.where(use)[0]}          # the slow part, done once\n",
    "    rows = []\n",
    "    for T in Ts:\n",
    "        ours = np.array([void_stats(ctx, i, extract_void_mask(ctx, i, T=T, resid=resid[i]))[\"void_ratio\"] for i in resid])\n",
    "        ref = csv[list(resid)]\n",
    "        rows.append(dict(T=T, mae=100 * np.abs(ours - ref).mean(), r=np.corrcoef(ours, ref)[0, 1],\n",
    "                         mean_ours=100 * ours.mean(), mean_csv=100 * ref.mean()))\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# FC-SP3 as an example (about 30 s). The T with the smallest error is what VOID_T holds for this type.\n",
    "cal = calibrate_threshold(ctx)\n",
    "print(f\"best T for FC-SP3: {int(cal.loc[cal.mae.idxmin(), 'T'])}   (VOID_T = {VOID_T['FC-SP3']})\")\n",
    "cal.round(2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "calib-caveat-disclaimer",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "> **Calibration caveat:** `VOID_T` is calibrated on the **same CSV** that is used\n",
    "> for the threshold sweep — the Pearson *r* and MAE values reported by\n",
    "> `calibrate_threshold` are a **training fit**, not held-out performance.\n",
    "> A panel-split cross-validation (e.g. leave-one-panel-out) is needed\n",
    "> before claiming generalisation to unseen panels or LED types.\n",
    "> **Do not report these numbers as test-set metrics.**"
   ]
  },
