  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "95c36be5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Next steps\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Join target.** Merge `features_df` with `rth_start_end.csv` on `unit_id`, compute `TSC_fail` using Part II's FailCT(RI in R_th) ≡ 20%, and discretize to Class 1 / 2 / 3.\n",
    "2. **Baseline vs. spatial Random Forest (per §5.3 of the proposal).**\n",
    "   - Baseline features: `led_type` one-hot + `paste` one-hot + total void ratio (use `electrical_mean_void_area_frac` or add a joint-wide one).\n",
    "   - Spatial features: baseline + all `thermal_*` and `electrical_mean_*` columns.\n",
    "   - Cross-validated per-class F1; test whether spatial model improves significantly over baseline.\n",
    "3. **Void threshold.** `VOID_T` is calibrated per LED type against `Xray Void Ratio.csv` (see `calibrate_threshold`). Re-calibrate if the registration or the fit is changed.\n",
    "4. **(Optional) Per-pad electrical features.** For 3-pad LEDs with two electrical pads, you currently average them. If asymmetry matters (e.g. voids under cathode worse than under anode), replace `electrical_mean_*` with `electrical_a_*` / `electrical_b_*` indexed by pad position."
   ]
  }
